<description>
Fill each bottom-marked vertical column by propagating the next colored pixel below upward through background cells.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color.
- One or more non-background pixels in the bottom row mark the vertical columns to complete.
- Each marked column contains colored pixels, including its bottom marker, that define stacked vertical color bands.

Rule
- Keep all original pixels unchanged.
- In each marked column, scan from bottom to top while remembering the most recent non-background color.
- Replace every background pixel in that column with the remembered color, so each colored pixel extends upward until another colored pixel is reached.

Key insight
- The bottom-row markers identify the only columns that should be rewritten; the scattered colors in those columns are band endpoints, not isolated objects.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "non-background pixels in columns whose bottom cell is non-background",
  "path": "straight upward along the same marked column, stopping before the next original non-background pixel or at the top edge",
  "trajectory": "paint each background pixel on the upward segment with the source color",
  "transform": "keep all original pixels and all unmarked columns unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 7-17 rows x same cols (always square), bg=0
  marked_columns:
    count: 1-3
    marker: bottom row (row H-1) has color 5 (gray); color 5 appears ONLY here
    spacing: >=3 columns apart [observed]
    input_pixels: 2-5 non-bg pixels per column (including bottom-row gray-5)
    output_bands: 2-4 contiguous color bands filling entire column top-to-bottom; bottom band is always gray-5; band height 1-13 rows
  input_pixel_placement: |
    Each output band has exactly 1 input pixel at its bottom row.
    ~11% of bands get a second redundant interior pixel of the same color.
    Consecutive bands may share a color (observed in ~30% of columns).
  noise_pixels:
    scattered single non-bg pixels in unmarked columns, density 0-17%
    color 5 never used in noise [observed]; colors may overlap with band colors
  output_rule: |
    Scan each marked column bottom-to-top; track current color (starts at bottom pixel).
    Replace each bg cell with current color; update current when hitting a non-bg pixel.
    Result: each band's color propagates upward through bg gaps to row 0 or next band pixel.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N in [7..17]; create NxN grid of bg=0.
    2. Pick K=1-3 marked columns, spaced >=3 apart.
    3. For each marked column, build OUTPUT column top-to-bottom:
       - Pick B=2-4 distinct colors (last = gray 5, others from 1-9 excl 5).
       - Partition N rows into B contiguous bands (each >=1 row).
    4. Derive INPUT from output: for each band, place 1 pixel at its bottom row;
       optionally add a second interior pixel (~10% chance per band, only if band height >=3).
       Rest of column is bg.
    5. Scatter noise pixels (0-17% of unmarked cells), no color 5, in unmarked columns.
```
